{"path":"io/basic_istream/unget","title":"std::basic_istream<CharT,Traits>::unget","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::basic_istream&lt;CharT,Traits&gt;::</span>unget","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/io/basic_istream/unget","section":"io","kind":"page","summary":"Makes the most recently extracted character available again.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">basic_istream<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> unget<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Makes the most recently extracted character available again.\n</p><p><span class=\"t-rev-inl t-since-cxx11\"><span>First, clears <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/ios_base/iostate\"><code>eofbit</code></a>. Then,</span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span></span></span> <code>unget</code> behaves as <a href=\"/w/cpp/named_req/UnformattedInputFunction\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">UnformattedInputFunction</em></a>. After constructing and checking the sentry object, if any <span class=\"t-lc\">ios_base::iostate</span> flags are set, the function sets <code>failbit</code> and returns. Otherwise, calls <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">rdbuf<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>sungetc<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.\n</p><p>If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">rdbuf<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>sungetc<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> returns <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">Traits<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">eof</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>, calls <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">setstate<span class=\"br0\">(</span>badbit<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.\n</p><p>In any case, sets the <code>gcount()</code> counter to zero.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this</span></code>\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Exceptions\">Exceptions</h3>\n<span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/ios_base/failure\">failure</a></span> if an error occurred (the error state flag is not <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/ios_base/iostate\">goodbit</a></span>) and <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_ios/exceptions\">exceptions()</a></span> is set to throw for that state.\n<p>If an internal operation throws an exception, it is caught and <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/ios_base/iostate\">badbit</a></span> is set. If <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_ios/exceptions\">exceptions()</a></span> is set for <code>badbit</code>, the exception is rethrown.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;sstream&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_istringstream\"><span class=\"kw1752\">std::<span class=\"me2\">istringstream</span></span></a> s1<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"Hello, world.\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">char</span> c1 <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> s1.<span class=\"me1\">get</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">if</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>s1.<span class=\"me1\">unget</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        <span class=\"kw4\">char</span> c2 <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> s1.<span class=\"me1\">get</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"Got: '\"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> c1 <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"'. Got again: '\"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> c2 <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"'.<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>Got: 'H'. Got again: 'H'.</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_streambuf/sungetc\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>sungetc</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  moves the next pointer in the input sequence back by one <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function of <code>std::basic_streambuf&lt;CharT,Traits&gt;</code>)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_istream/get\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>get</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  extracts characters <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_istream/peek\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>peek</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  reads the next character without extracting it <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_istream/putback\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>putback</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  puts a character into input stream <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Exceptions","id":"Exceptions"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"io","title":"Input/output library"},{"path":"io/basic_istream","title":"std::basic_istream"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::basic_istream<CharT,Traits>::unget","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. Makes the most recently extracted character available again."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Return value","note":"*this"},{"label":"Exceptions","note":"if an error occurred (the error state flag is not"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"sungetc","note":"moves the next pointer in the input sequence back by one"},{"label":"get","note":"extracts characters"},{"label":"peek","note":"reads the next character without extracting it"},{"label":"putback","note":"puts a character into input stream"}]}]},"standards":["C++11"],"wordCount":198,"codeBlockCount":2}
